  era: "c. 1163\u20131323 \xB7 Section 13 \xB7 South Indian Kingdoms \xB7 c. 850 \u2013 1650 CE"
  title: Kakatiyas
  text: The Kakatiyas ruled Telangana and Andhra from Warangal in the 12th to 14th centuries. Rudramadevi was one of India's few reigning queens. The Ramappa temple is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and their lake tanks supported farming.
